+## Using installed dependencies
+
+By default the build downloads and compiles every dependency at the version
+pinned in `CMakeLists.txt`, which is what the release binaries are built from.
+A distribution package, or any build without network access, can use the
+system's copies instead:
+
+    cmake --preset default -DEXTEMPORE_SYSTEM_DEPS=ON
+
+Nothing is downloaded then, and these have to be installed:
+
+- LLVM in the pinned release series (22.1 at present), with its CMake package
+  and its static component libraries (`llvm-static` on Fedora). Any 22.1.x is
+  accepted. Extempore links the components statically, as it does its own.
+- PCRE2 and PortAudio, found through `pkg-config` (`libpcre2-8`,
+  `portaudio-2.0`).
+- portmidi, rtmidi, libsndfile and Extempore's
+  [fork of KISS FFT](https://github.com/extemporelang/kiss_fft), as shared
+  libraries. They are linked into `libs/platform-shlibs` rather than copied,
+  since that is where the xtlang bindings load them from.
+- GoogleTest, when `BUILD_TESTS` is on.
+
+`JACK` and `EXTERNAL_SHLIBS_GRAPHICS` are refused alongside it: the installed
+PortAudio's backends are whatever it was built with, and the WebGPU stack is
+still downloaded only.
+
